-total\">16 or 17 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-fall\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Fall</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"mathematics-ba__box-2-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;College Calculus 3&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Geometry and vectors of n-dimensional space; Green\\u2019s theorem, Gauss theorem, Stokes theorem; multidimensional differentiation and integration; application to 2- and 3-D space.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer, Winter&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: MTH 142 or MTH 154 or MTH 138 and MTH 139 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: true, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8181&amp;returnto=1177&quot;, &quot;groups&quot;: [{&quot;requirement_type&quot;: &quot;choice_required&quot;, &quot;group&quot;: &quot;Mathematics - General Curriculum Core - Calculus 3 (choose 1 of 2)&quot;, &quot;courses&quot;: [{&quot;code&quot;: &quot;MTH 241LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;College Calculus 3&quot;}, {&quot;code&quot;: &quot;MTH 251LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Honors Calculus 3&quot;}]}]}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">full list on click</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Mathematics - General Curriculum Core - Calculus 3 (choose 1 of 2)</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"mathematics-ba__box-2-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Introductory Linear Algebra&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Linear equations, matrices, determinants, vector spaces, linear mappings, inner products, eigenvalues, eigenvectors.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: MTH 142 or MTH 154 or MTH 138 and MTH 139&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: true, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8181&amp;returnto=1177&quot;, &quot;groups&quot;: [{&quot;requirement_type&quot;: &quot;choice_required&quot;, &quot;group&quot;: &quot;Mathematics - General Curriculum Core - Linear Algebra (choose 1 of 2)&quot;, &quot;courses&quot;: [{&quot;code&quot;: &quot;MTH 309LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Introductory Linear Algebra&quot;}, {&quot;code&quot;: &quot;MTH 323LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Honors Linear Algebra&quot;}]}]}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">full list on click</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Mathematics - General Curriculum Core - Linear Algebra (choose 1 of 2)</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"mathematics-ba__box-2-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Scientific Literacy and Inquiry: a 7-credit UB Curriculum Foundations requirement (two lecture courses plus a matching 1-credit lab from the same subject area).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/foundations.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Scientific Literacy and Inquiry 1</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"mathematics-ba__box-2-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Scientific Literacy and Inquiry: a 7-credit UB Curriculum Foundations requirement (two lecture courses plus a matching 1-credit lab from the same subject area).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/foundations.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Scientific Literacy and Inquiry Lab</div><span class=\"box-credits\">1 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"mathematics-ba__box-2-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">15 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-spring\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Spring</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"mathematics-ba__box-3-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Introduction to Differential Equations&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Analytic solutions, qualitative behavior of solutions to differential equations. First-order and higher-order ordinary differential equations, including nonlinear equations. Covers analytic, geometric, and numerical perspectives as well as an interplay between methods and model problems. Discusses necessary matrix theory and explores differential equation models of phenomena from various disciplines. Uses a mathematical software system designed to aid in the numerical and qualitative study of solutions, and in the geometric interpretation of solutions.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: MTH 142 or MTH 154 or MTH 138 and MTH 139 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: true, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8181&amp;returnto=1177&quot;, &quot;groups&quot;: [{&quot;requirement_type&quot;: &quot;choice_required&quot;, &quot;group&quot;: &quot;Mathematics - General Curriculum Core - Differential Equations (choose 1 of 2)&quot;, &quot;courses&quot;: [{&quot;code&quot;: &quot;MTH 306LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Introduction to Differential Equations&quot;}, {&quot;code&quot;: &quot;MTH 326LR&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Honors Diff Equations&quot;}]}]}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">full list on click</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Mathematics - General Curriculum Core - Differential Equations (choose 1 of 2)</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"mathematics-ba__box-3-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Introduction to Higher Mathematics&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Develops the student\\u2019s ability to read, comprehend and construct rigorous proofs. Topics may include the following: the number systems N, Z, Q, R and the existence of irrational numbers; sets and functions; size of sets(finite/infinite, countable/uncountable); the countability of the rationals and the uncountability of the real numbers; boundedness; upper and lower bounds; lub\\u2019s and glb\\u2019s; lub and glb property; density of the rationals in the reals; Archimedean property of the reals; mathematical induction, including strong induction and the well-ordering of the natural numbers; sequences of real numbers, including the Monotone Convergence Theorem, Cauchy sequences, and the Bolzano-Weierstrass Theorem.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: MTH 241 or MTH 251 or Permission of Instructor.&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">MTH 311LR</span><span class=\"box-title\">Introduction to Higher Mathematics</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"mathematics-ba__box-3-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"mathematics-ba__box-3-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: 